lregister.gov/documents/2026/09/15/2026-18873/commission-information-collection-activities-ferc-561-comment-request-extension","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-09-15/pdf/2026-18873.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-18873.pdf?1789389919","publication_date":"2026-09-15","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF ENERGY","name":"Energy Department","id":136,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/energy-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/136","parent_id":null,"slug":"energy-department"},{"raw_name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","id":167,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-energy-regulatory-commission","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/167","parent_id":136,"slug":"federal-energy-regulatory-commission"}],"excerpts":"In compliance with the requirements of the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (Commission or FERC) is soliciting public comment on the currently approved information collection FERC-561 (OMB Control No...."},{"title":"Commission Information Collection Activities (FERC-912); Comment Request; Extension","type":"Notice","abstract":"In compliance with the requirements of the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (Commission or FERC) is soliciting public comment on the currently approved information collection FERC-912 (1902-0237), PURPA Section 210(m) Notification Requirements Applicable to Cogeneration and Small Power Production Facilities. The comment period ended on September 8, 2026, with no comments received. There are no changes to the reporting requirements.","document_number":"2026-18872","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/15/2026-18872/commission-information-collection-activities-ferc-912-comment-request-extension","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-09-15/pdf/2026-18872.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-18872.pdf?1789389919","publication_date":"2026-09-15","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF ENERGY","name":"Energy Department","id":136,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/energy-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/136","parent_id":null,"slug":"energy-department"},{"raw_name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","id":167,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-energy-regulatory-commission","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/167","parent_id":136,"slug":"federal-energy-regulatory-commission"}],"excerpts":"In compliance with the requirements of the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (Commission or FERC) is soliciting public comment on the currently approved information collection FERC-912 (1902-0237), PURPA Section..."},{"title":"Commission Information Collection Activities (FERC-556); Comment Request; Extension","type":"Notice","abstract":"In compliance with the requirements of the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (Commission or FERC) is soliciting public comment on the currently approved information collection FERC-556 (OMB Control No. 1902-0075) Certification of Qualifying Facility (QF) Status for a Small Power Production or Cogeneration Facility. The comment period ended on September 8, 2026, with no comments received. There were no changes to the reporting requirements.","document_number":"2026-18871","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/15/2026-18871/commission-information-collection-activities-ferc-556-comment-request-extension","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-09-15/pdf/2026-18871.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-18871.pdf?1789389918","publication_date":"2026-09-15","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF ENERGY","name":"Energy Department","id":136,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/energy-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/136","parent_id":null,"slug":"energy-department"},{"raw_name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","id":167,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-energy-regulatory-commission","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/167","parent_id":136,"slug":"federal-energy-regulatory-commission"}],"excerpts":"In compliance with the requirements of the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (Commission or FERC) is soliciting public comment on the currently approved information collection FERC-556 (OMB Control No. 1902-0075)..."},{"title":"Commission Information Collection Activities (FERC-549D); Comment Request; Extension","type":"Notice","abstract":"In compliance with the requirements of the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (Commission or FERC) is soliciting public comment on the currently approved information collection, FERC-549D (OMB Control No. 1902-0253), Quarterly Transportation and Storage Report for Intrastate Natural Gas and Hinshaw Pipelines. The comment period ended on September 8, 2026, with no comments received. There were no changes to the reporting requirements.","document_number":"2026-18870","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/15/2026-18870/commission-information-collection-activities-ferc-549d-comment-request-extension","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-09-15/pdf/2026-18870.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-18870.pdf?1789389918","publication_date":"2026-09-15","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF ENERGY","name":"Energy Department","id":136,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/energy-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/136","parent_id":null,"slug":"energy-department"},{"raw_name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","id":167,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-energy-regulatory-commission","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/167","parent_id":136,"slug":"federal-energy-regulatory-commission"}],"excerpts":"In compliance with the requirements of the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (Commission or FERC) is soliciting public comment on the currently approved information collection, FERC-549D (OMB Control No...."},{"title":"Dominion Energy South Carolina, Inc.; Notice of Availability of Environmental Assessment","type":"Notice","abstract":null,"document_number":"2026-18869","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/15/2026-18869/dominion-energy-south-carolina-inc-notice-of-availability-of-environmental-assessment","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-09-15/pdf/2026-18869.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-18869.pdf?1789389918","publication_date":"2026-09-15","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF ENERGY","name":"Energy Department","id":136,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/energy-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/136","parent_id":null,"slug":"energy-department"},{"raw_name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","id":167,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-energy-regulatory-commission","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/167","parent_id":136,"slug":"federal-energy-regulatory-commission"}],"excerpts":null},{"title":"North American Electric Reliability Corporation; Order Approving Reliability Standard CIP-014-4","type":"Notice","abstract":null,"document_number":"2026-18868","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/15/2026-18868/north-american-electric-reliability-corporation-order-approving-reliability-standard-cip-014-4","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-09-15/pdf/2026-18868.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-18868.pdf?1789389918","publication_date":"2026-09-15","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF ENERGY","name":"Energy Department","id":136,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/energy-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/136","parent_id":null,"slug":"energy-department"},{"raw_name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","name":"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission","id":167,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-energy-regulatory-commission","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/167","parent_id":136,"slug":"federal-energy-regulatory-commission"}],"excerpts":null},{"title":"Agency Information Collection Activities; Submission to the Office of Management and Budget for Review and Approval; Request for Comment; Criminal Penalty Safe Harbor Provision","type":"Notice","abstract":"In compliance with the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 (PRA), this notice announces that the Information Collection Request (ICR) summarized below will be submitted to the Office of Management and Budget (OMB) for review and approval. The ICR describes the nature of the information collection and its expected burden. This collection of information for which NHTSA seeks OMB approval concerns NHTSA's Criminal Penalty Safe Harbor Provision. NHTSA previously requested and received a three-year approval of this information collection. NHTSA now requests OMB's approval for a three-year reinstatement of this previously approved information collection. NHTSA published a notice on May 29, 2026 requesting comment on the reinstatement of this ICR. NHTSA received no public comments in response to the notice.","document_number":"2026-18867","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/15/2026-18867/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-for","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-09-15/pdf/2026-18867.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-18867.pdf?1789389918","publication_date":"2026-09-15","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION","name":"Transportation Department","id":492,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/transportation-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/492","parent_id":null,"slug":"transportation-department"},{"raw_name":"National Highway Traffic Safety Administration","name":"National Highway Traffic Safety Administration","id":345,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/national-highway-traffic-safety-administration","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/345","parent_id":492,"slug":"national-highway-traffic-safety-administration"}],"excerpts":"In compliance with the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 (PRA), this notice announces that the Information Collection Request (ICR) summarized below will be submitted to the Office of Management and Budget (OMB) for review and approval. The ICR describes..."},{"title":"Establishment of United States Area Navigation Route T-337 and Amendment of Very High Frequency Omnidirectional Range Federal Airways V-101 and V-484 Near Twin Falls, ID","type":"Proposed Rule","abstract":"This action proposes to establish United States Area Navigation (RNAV) route T-337 and amend Very High Frequency (VHF) Omnidirectional Range (VOR) federal airways V-101 and V-484 near Twin Falls, ID. The FAA is proposing this action due to the pending decommissioning of the Hailey, ID, Nondirectional Radio Beacon (NDB)/ Distance Measuring Equipment (DME).","document_number":"2026-18860","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/15/2026-18860/establishment-of-united-states-area-navigation-route-t-337-and-amendment-of-very-high-frequency","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-09-15/pdf/2026-18860.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-18860.pdf?1789389917","publication_date":"2026-09-15","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION","name":"Transportation Department","id":492,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/transportation-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/492","parent_id":null,"slug":"transportation-department"},{"raw_name":"Federal Aviation Administration","name":"Federal Aviation Administration","id":159,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-aviation-administration","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/159","parent_id":492,"slug":"federal-aviation-administration"}],"excerpts":"This action proposes to establish United States Area Navigation (RNAV) route T-337 and amend Very High Frequency (VHF) Omnidirectional Range (VOR) federal airways V-101 and V-484 near Twin Falls, ID. The FAA is proposing this action due to the pending..."},{"title":"Airworthiness Directives; Airbus Defence and Space GmbH Airplanes","type":"Proposed Rule","abstract":"The FAA proposes to adopt a new airworthiness directive (AD) for all Airbus Defence and Space GmbH Model BO-209-150 FF, BO-209-150 FV, BO-209-150 RV, BO-209-160 FV, BO-209-160 RV, and B[ouml]lkow Jr. airplanes. This proposed AD was prompted by reports of corrosion damage on the rudder drive. This proposed AD would require repetitive inspections of the rudder drive, corrective actions including replacement if corrosion is detected and the application of a corrosion inhibitor. This proposed AD would also prohibit the installation of affected parts. The FAA is proposing this AD to address the unsafe condition on these products.","document_number":"2026-18850","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/15/2026-18850/airworthiness-directives-airbus-defence-and-space-gmbh-airplanes","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-09-15/pdf/2026-18850.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-18850.pdf?1789389916","publication_date":"2026-09-15","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION","name":"Transportation Department","id":492,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/transportation-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/492","parent_id":null,"slug":"transportation-department"},{"raw_name":"Federal Aviation Administration","name":"Federal Aviation Administration","id":159,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-aviation-administration","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/159","parent_id":492,"slug":"federal-aviation-administration"}],"excerpts":"The FAA proposes to adopt a new airworthiness directive (AD) for all Airbus Defence and Space GmbH Model BO-209-150 FF, BO-209-150 FV, BO-209-150 RV, BO-209-160 FV, BO-209-160 RV, and B[ouml]lkow Jr. airplanes. This proposed AD was prompted by reports..."},{"title":"Pacific Island Fisheries; Catch and Retention Limits for Striped Marlin in the Western and Central Pacific Ocean North of the Equator","type":"Rule","abstract":"This final rule implements a framework for specifying catch limits for all U.S. fisheries and retention limits by U.S. longline fisheries under a Hawaii longline limited entry permit for Western and Central North Pacific Ocean (WCNPO) striped marlin (Kajikia audax), consistent with the requirements of Western and Central Pacific Fisheries Commission (WCPFC) Conservation and Management Measure (CMM) 2024-06. If the retention limit is reached, NMFS will prohibit retention of WCNPO striped marlin by longline fishing vessels until the end of the year to prevent the U.S. catch limit from being exceeded. Because the U.S. limit under the framework can change each year, NMFS will specify the updated catch and longline retention limits by notice in the Federal Register early each calendar year. For fishing year 2026, NMFS specifies a U.S. WCNPO striped marlin limit of 393.4 metric tons (mt) (867,300 pounds (lb)) and a U.S. longline retention limit of 381.6 mt (841,300 lb) using the framework.","document_number":"2026-18849","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/15/2026-18849/pacific-island-fisheries-catch-and-retention-limits-for-striped-marlin-in-the-western-and-central","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-09-15/pdf/2026-18849.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-18849.pdf?1789389916","publication_date":"2026-09-15","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE","name":"Commerce Department","id":54,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/commerce-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/54","parent_id":null,"slug":"commerce-department"},{"raw_name":"National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration","name":"National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration","id":361,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/national-oceanic-and-atmospheric-administration","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/361","parent_id":54,"slug":"national-oceanic-and-atmospheric-administration"}],"excerpts":"This final rule implements a framework for specifying catch limits for all U.S. fisheries and retention limits by U.S. longline fisheries under a Hawaii longline limited entry permit for Western and Central North Pacific Ocean (WCNPO) striped marlin..."}]}